{
 "about": "Transcript lines and the time each reader must give for a turn that ended past the mark with no hook to say so: runs.py ended (test_runs E11) and Runs.swift turnEnded (test_runs.sh R18). A case is written as its lines, each ending in a newline, then, when pad is set, a line of that many x characters; mark counts the lines written before the run began; at is the end's time, null for none, or \"mtime\" for the transcript's modification time, which each suite sets to 1700000000 once the file is written. An Esc line ends the turn at its stamp; the main agent's last assistant line, a subagent's (isSidechain) skipped, if its message ended its turn, ends it at its stamp once now, when a case names it, is six seconds past, whatever user lines follow it; a case with no now is read at the time it runs.",
